# function pick(flag, a, b) { return flag ? a : b }  print(pick(true, "first", "second")); print(pick(false, "first", "second"))
# The table of origins says that `pick` answers its second or its third parameter and nothing else.
# A validating build tests that behind each call, on the values that the call passes: `result === a | result === b`, and the process ends where neither holds. NaN is equal to nothing and passes.
# It judges what the link makes of the records. A record that leaves out a value that is returned does not get this far: the verifier of the relations refuses it when the program is built
# FORM: AsRead
# RUN: valueflow-apply
# RUN(RUNS): run-in-shell void 0;
# OPTIONS: validate
# CHECK: v4: string = Call v0, -, v3, v1, v2
# CHECK-NEXT: = StrictEq v4, v4
# CHECK-NEXT: = LogicalNot
# CHECK-NEXT: = StrictEq v4, v1
# CHECK-NEXT: = BitOr
# CHECK-NEXT: = StrictEq v4, v2
# CHECK-NEXT: = BitOr
# CHECK-NEXT: = ToBoolean
# CHECK-NEXT: = Boolean boolean=true
# CHECK-NEXT: ValidateSameValue
# RUNS: first
# RUNS-NEXT: second
# RUNS-NOT: AOT validation
# RUNS: exited with 0

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js" body=f0
entry module=m0
function f0 name="main" kind=Module results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    v0 = NewClosure function=f1
    v1 = String string="first"
    v2 = String string="second"
    v3 = Boolean boolean=true
    v4 = Call v0, -, v3, v1, v2
    v5 = Builtin builtin=GlobalThis
    v6 = PropGet v5 key="print" [isFreeName]
    v7 = Call v6, -, v4
    v8 = Boolean boolean=false
    v9 = Call v0, -, v8, v1, v2
    v10 = Call v6, -, v9
    Return
}
function f1 name="pick" parameters=[{type=anything}, {type=anything}, {type=anything}] results=[{type=anything}] relations={subjects=[{}, {index=1 fate=[IsReturned] results=1}, {index=2 fate=[IsReturned] results=1}] resultsFullyListed=1} {
  b0(v0: anything, v1: anything, v2: anything):
    v3 = ToBoolean v0
    Branch v3 -> taken b1(), notTaken b2()
  b1():
    Return v1
  b2():
    Return v2
}
